  <section class="section" id="optimization">
    <h2><span class="sec-num">6</span> Optimization Insights &amp; Recommendations</h2>
    <p class="sec-obj">Synthesize findings into actionable recommendations for load balancing, queue management, pricing strategy, and renewable energy maximization.</p>

    <h3 style="font-size:0.95rem;margin:0 0 14px;font-weight:600;">Cross-Cutting Findings</h3>
    <ul class="insight-list">
      <li class="warn">Peak-to-Off-Peak grid load differential is 142.6% (84.07 kW vs. 34.65 kW), but wait times are flat across time slots &mdash; capacity exists to shift demand.</li>
      <li class="good">Off-Peak sessions have 35% higher renewable energy ratios than Peak (39.3% vs. 29.0%), and 30.1% of Off-Peak sessions exceed 50% renewable vs. just 8.8% during Peak.</li>
      <li class="warn">Dynamic pricing is effectively flat (9.94&ndash;9.97 across time slots) and shows zero meaningful correlation with demand or renewable availability &mdash; a major policy gap.</li>
      <li class="bad">Peak optimization reward is &minus;19.80 vs. Off-Peak at &minus;7.06, confirming Peak sessions generate nearly 3&times; worse grid outcomes.</li>
      <li class="good">Vehicle types and location types show minimal behavioral differences, enabling uniform policy interventions across the fleet.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem;margin:24px 0 14px;font-weight:700;">Recommendations</h3>
    <div class="rec-grid">

      <div class="rec-card high">
        <div class="rec-title">1. Implement Time-of-Use Pricing</div>
        <div class="rec-body">Introduce meaningful price differentials between Peak and Off-Peak windows. Current pricing is flat at ~9.96 across all slots. A 20&ndash;30% Off-Peak discount (targeting ~7.50&ndash;8.00) would create economic incentives aligned with the 142.6% load differential and 35% higher renewable availability during Off-Peak.</div>
        <div class="rec-impact" style="color:#e65100;">High Priority &middot; Estimated impact: 15&ndash;25% Peak demand reduction</div>
      </div>

      <div class="rec-card high">
        <div class="rec-title">2. Green Charging Incentive Program</div>
        <div class="rec-body">Offer a "Green Charging" discount when renewable ratios exceed 50%. Off-Peak already delivers this in 30.1% of sessions vs. 8.8% during Peak. Price at a premium when renewable ratio is below 25% (mostly Peak). This directly ties cost to sustainability outcomes.</div>
        <div class="rec-impact" style="color:#e65100;">High Priority &middot; Estimated impact: 10&ndash;20% shift to high-renewable windows</div>
      </div>

      <div class="rec-card medium">
        <div class="rec-title">3. Load-Shifting Campaigns for Off-Peak</div>
        <div class="rec-body">62.5% of sessions already occur Off-Peak, but they carry only 34.65 kW average load vs. 84.07 kW during Peak. Target flexible chargers (Two-Wheelers with shorter sessions) through app notifications and scheduled charging features to fill Off-Peak capacity without increasing Peak demand.</div>
        <div class="rec-impact" style="color:#1a73e8;">Medium Priority &middot; Estimated impact: 8&ndash;12% Peak load reduction</div>
      </div>

      <div class="rec-card medium">
        <div class="rec-title">4. Smart Queue Prioritization</div>
        <div class="rec-body">While wait times are currently manageable (~9.5 min average), implement priority queuing for sessions with high renewable energy availability. When renewable ratio &gt;50%, fast-track vehicles to chargers. This maximizes green energy capture and improves the optimization reward metric from its current &minus;11.83 baseline.</div>
        <div class="rec-impact" style="color:#1a73e8;">Medium Priority &middot; Estimated impact: 5&ndash;10% improvement in optimization reward</div>
      </div>

      <div class="rec-card low">
        <div class="rec-title">5. Station-Level Capacity Rebalancing</div>
        <div class="rec-body">Top stations (ST013, ST001, ST012) carry disproportionate demand. Evaluate adding charger capacity at these stations or redirecting traffic to lower-utilization stations. Current queue lengths (4.5&ndash;4.8 avg) suggest moderate congestion that could worsen with demand growth.</div>
        <div class="rec-impact" style="color:#00c853;">Lower Priority &middot; Estimated impact: Preventive &mdash; future-proofing</div>
      </div>

      <div class="rec-card low">
        <div class="rec-title">6. Weather-Aware Scheduling</div>
        <div class="rec-body">Clear-weather Off-Peak periods achieve the highest renewable ratios (39.7%). Integrate weather forecasts into the scheduling system to proactively offer "sunny day discounts" and encourage charging when renewable supply is forecasted to be strongest.</div>
        <div class="rec-impact" style="color:#00c853;">Lower Priority &middot; Estimated impact: 3&ndash;5% renewable ratio improvement</div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="takeaway">
      <strong>Key Takeaway</strong>
      The network's primary optimization lever is temporal: shifting demand from Peak to Off-Peak simultaneously reduces grid stress by up to 142.6%, improves renewable energy capture by 35%, and nearly triples the optimization reward. The current flat pricing structure is the single biggest policy gap. Implementing time-of-use pricing with a green-charging incentive would align economic signals with grid and sustainability objectives, potentially moving 15&ndash;25% of Peak demand to Off-Peak windows.
    </div>
